{"step_index":46,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T10:23:35Z","input_tokens":2943,"cache_read_tokens":134904,"output_tokens":15709,"thinking":"Focusing on the separation of frontend modules, the objective is to ensure the UI, Execution Engine, Rule-Based System, and UI Controller operate independently and completely offline. A careful examination of the Execution Engine's requirements is crucial.\n\n\n`class Solution:` introduces a class named `Solution`. Python interprets this as a blueprint for creating objects of this type; it doesn't execute any code directly at this stage, only defines a structure.\n\n\nThe `maxSubArray` method definition registers within the `Solution` class; execution is deferred until a call is made with specific input. The program will initialize `ans` to the first element of the input array, `nums`, and `c` will track the current subarray sum. This initialization ensures a proper baseline for handling arrays with all negative numbers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// engine.js — Separated Python AST Support Checker & Real Step-by-Step Execution Engine\n// 100% Local & Deterministic. No AI APIs.\n\nconst PRELOADED_PROGRAMS = {\n  max_subarray: {\n    title: \"1. Maximum Subarray (Kadane's Algorithm — Default)\",\n    defaultInput: \"nums = [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"Finds the maximum sum of a contiguous, non-empty subarray. Variable `c` tracks the current candidate subarray sum, and `ans` tracks the best (maximum) sum found so far. Initializing `ans = nums[0]` ensures the algorithm works correctly even when all numbers in `nums` are negative. Whenever `c < 0`, resetting `c = 0` discards the negative prefix because adding a negative sum to the next subarray would only make its sum smaller.\",\n    code: `class Solution:\n    def maxSubArray(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:\n        c = 0\n        ans = nums[0]\n\n        for i in range(len(nums)):\n            c += nums[i]\n\n            if c >= ans:\n                ans = c\n\n            if c < 0:\n                c = 0\n\n        return ans`\n  },\n  nested_loops: {\n    title: \"2. Nested Loops: Pair Sum Counter\",\n    defaultInput: \"nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"Demonstrates nested `for` loops and conditions: for each index `i`, the inner loop checks every later index `j` and counts how many pairs have an even sum.\",\n    code: `pairs = 0\ntotal = 0\n\nfor i in range(len(nums)):\n    for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):\n        pair_sum = nums[i] + nums[j]\n        if pair_sum % 2 == 0:\n            pairs += 1\n            total += pair_sum\n\nprint(\"Even pairs:\", pairs)\nprint(\"Total sum:\", total)`\n  },\n  recursion_factorial: {\n    title: \"3. Recursion & Functions: Factorial\",\n    defaultInput: \"n = 4\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"Demonstrates functions, arguments, parameters, recursive calls, and return values unwinding on the Call Stack.\",\n    code: `def factorial(k: int) -> int:\n    if k <= 1:\n        return 1\n    sub = factorial(k - 1)\n    return k * sub\n\nans = factorial(n)\nprint(\"Factorial is:\", ans)`\n  },\n  break_continue_loop: {\n    title: \"4. Loop Control: break and continue\",\n    defaultInput: \"nums = [3, -1, 5, 0, 99, 4]\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"Shows how `continue` skips negative numbers and moves to the next iteration, while `break` exits the loop immediately when `99` is encountered.\",\n    code: `valid_sum = 0\nchecked = 0\n\nfor x in nums:\n    if x < 0:\n        continue\n    if x == 99:\n        break\n    valid_sum += x\n    checked += 1\n\nprint(\"Valid sum:\", valid_sum)`\n  }\n};\n\nclass PythonExecutionEngine {\n  constructor() {\n    this.maxSteps = 400;\n  }\n\n  validateSupport(sourceCode) {\n    if (!sourceCode || !sourceCode.trim()) {\n      return {\n        ok: false,\n        line: 1,\n        message: \"The code editor is empty. Paste or write a Python program to analyze.\"\n      };\n    }\n\n    const lines = sourceCode.replace(/\\r\\n/g, \"\\n\").split(\"\\n\");\n\n    const unsupportedRules = [\n      { regex: /^\\s*(import|from)\\s+/, msg: \"`import` statements are not supported in the offline sandbox.\" },\n      { regex: /^\\s*async\\s+/, msg: \"`async` / `await` constructs are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\bawait\\s+/, msg: \"`await` expressions are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /^\\s*with\\s+/, msg: \"`with` context managers and file I/O are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\byield\\b/, msg: \"Generator `yield` statements are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\blambda\\b/, msg: \"`lambda` expressions are not supported; please use `def`.\" },\n      { regex: /^\\s*(try|except|finally)\\b/, msg: \"`try / except` blocks are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\b(open|eval|exec|__import__|input)\\s*\\(/, msg: \"Restricted built-in function (`open`, `eval`, `exec`, `input`) is disabled for security.\" }\n    ];\n\n    let parenDepth = 0;\n    let bracketDepth = 0;\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\n      const raw = lines[i];\n      const stripped = this.stripInlineComment(raw);\n      const trimmed = stripped.trim();\n      if (!trimmed) continue;\n\n      for (const rule of unsupportedRules) {\n        if (rule.regex.test(trimmed)) {\n          return {\n            ok: false,\n            line: i + 1,\n            message: `Unsupported Syntax on Line ${i + 1}: ${rule.msg}`\n          };\n        }\n      }\n\n      // Check block header colons\n      if (/^(class|def|if|elif|else|for|while)\\b/.test(trimmed) && !trimmed.endsWith(\":\")) {\n        return {\n          ok: false,\n          line: i + 1,\n          message: `SyntaxError on Line ${i + 1}: Block header (\\`${trimmed}\\`) must end with a colon (\\`:\\`).`\n        };\n      }\n\n      for (const ch of trimmed) {\n        if (ch === \"(\") parenDepth++;\n        else if (ch === \")\") parenDepth--;\n        else if (ch === \"[\") bracketDepth++;\n        else if (ch === \"]\") bracketDepth--;\n      }\n\n      if (parenDepth < 0 || bracketDepth < 0) {\n        return {\n          ok: false,\n          line: i + 1,\n          message: `SyntaxError on Line ${i + 1}: Unmatched closing parenthesis or bracket.`\n        };\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (parenDepth !== 0 || bracketDepth !== 0) {\n      return {\n        ok: false,\n        line: lines.length,\n        message: \"SyntaxError: Unclosed parenthesis `(` or bracket `[` in code.\"\n      };\n    }\n\n    return { ok: true, line: null, message: null };\n  }\n\n  validateInputPlayground(inputStr) {\n    const trimmed = (inputStr || \"\").trim();\n    if (!trimmed) {\n      return {\n        ok: false,\n        message: \"Input Playground is empty. Please provide an input assignment such as `nums = [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]`.\"\n      };\n    }\n    const check = this.validateSupport(trimmed);\n    if (!check.ok) {\n      return { ok: false, message: `Invalid Input: ${check.message}` };\n    }\n    return { ok: true, message: null };\n  }\n\n  trace(sourceCode, inputCode = \"\") {\n    const validation = this.validateSupport(sourceCode);\n    const rawLines = sourceCode.replace(/\\r\\n/g, \"\\n\").split(\"\\n\");\n\n    if (!validation.ok) {\n      return {\n        ok: false,\n        errorType: \"UNSUPPORTED_OR_SYNTAX\",\n        errorMessage: validation.message,\n        errorLine: validation.line,\n        rawLines,\n        steps: [],\n        cfg: { nodes: [], edges: [] }\n      };\n    }\n\n    if (inputCode && inputCode.trim()) {\n      const inVal = this.validateInputPlayground(inputCode);\n      if (!inVal.ok) {\n        return {\n          ok: false,\n          errorType: \"INVALID_INPUT\",\n          errorMessage: inVal.message,\n          errorLine: 1,\n          rawLines,\n          steps: [],\n          cfg: { nodes: [], edges: [] }\n        };\n      }\n    }\n\n    const statements = this.parseProgram(rawLines);\n    const cfg = this.buildControlFlowGraph(statements);\n\n    const steps = [];\n    const stdout = [];\n    const functions = {};\n    const classes = {};\n    const callStack = [\n      {\n        frameName: \"Global Scope\",\n        vars: {},\n        prevVars: {}\n      }\n    ];\n    const loopStack = [];\n\n    // Seed input playground variables into initial environment if code doesn't define them on top\n    const inputVars = {};\n    if (inputCode && inputCode.trim()) {\n      try {\n        const inputStmts = this.parseProgram(inputCode.split(\"\\n\"));\n        const dummyFrame = { frameName: \"Input\", vars: {}, prevVars: {} };\n        for (const st of inputStmts) {\n          if (st.kind === \"STMT\" && st.text.includes(\"=\")) {\n            const eqIdx = st.text.indexOf(\"=\");\n            const vName = st.text.slice(0, eqIdx).trim();\n            const vExpr = st.text.slice(eqIdx + 1).trim();\n            dummyFrame.vars[vName] = this.evalExpr(vExpr, dummyFrame.vars, {}, [], [], [], [], 1);\n            inputVars[vName] = dummyFrame.vars[vName];\n          }\n        }\n      } catch (err) {\n        return {\n          ok: false,\n          errorType: \"INVALID_INPUT\",\n          errorMessage: `Invalid Input Playground expression: ${err.message || err}`,\n          errorLine: 1,\n          rawLines,\n          steps: [],\n          cfg\n        };\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Bind input playground variables into Global Scope if not overwritten\n    Object.entries(inputVars).forEach(([k, v]) => {\n      callStack[0].vars[k] = Array.isArray(v) ? [...v] : v;\n      callStack[0].prevVars[k] = Array.isArray(v) ? [...v] : v;\n    });\n\n    let finalReturnVal = null;\n\n    try {\n      this.executeSuite(statements, callStack, functions, classes, steps, stdout, loopStack);\n\n      // If the program defined `class Solution:` with a method (e.g., `maxSubArray`) and didn't call it in top-level statements, invoke it now!\n      const hasClassSolution = Boolean(classes[\"Solution\"]);\n      const solMethods = hasClassSolution ? Object.keys(classes[\"Solution\"].methods) : [];\n      if (hasClassSolution && solMethods.length > 0 && steps.length <= 3) {\n        const methodName = solMethods[0];\n        const fnNode = classes[\"Solution\"].methods[methodName];\n        const paramName = fnNode.params[0] || \"nums\";\n        const argVal =\n          paramName in inputVars\n            ? inputVars[paramName]\n            : Object.values(inputVars)[0] !== undefined\n            ? Object.values(inputVars)[0]\n            : [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4];\n\n        const callRes = this.invokeFunctionNode(\n          fnNode,\n          [argVal],\n          [paramName],\n          callStack,\n          functions,\n          classes,\n          steps,\n          stdout,\n          loopStack,\n          fnNode.line\n        );\n        if (callRes && callRes.returned) {\n          finalReturnVal = callRes.value;\n        }\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      const errLine = err.line || 1;\n      const errMsg = err.message || String(err);\n      steps.push({\n        stepIndex: steps.length + 1,\n        line: errLine,\n        nextLine: null,\n        codeText: rawLines[errLine - 1] ? rawLines[errLine - 1].trim() : \"\",\n        eventType: \"EXCEPTION\",\n        functionName: callStack[callStack.length - 1].frameName,\n        beforeVars: this.cloneVarsMap(callStack[callStack.length - 1].vars),\n        variables: this.buildInspectorRows(callStack[callStack.length - 1].vars, null),\n        changedVars: [],\n        changedSummary: `Exception raised: ${errMsg}`,\n        condition: null,\n        loop: this.getCurrentLoopSnapshot(loopStack),\n        operationDetail: { kind: \"exception\", message: errMsg },\n        returnValue: null,\n        stdout: [...stdout]\n      });\n\n      this.finalizeNextLines(steps);\n      return {\n        ok: false,\n        errorType: \"RUNTIME_EXCEPTION\",\n        errorMessage: errMsg,\n        errorLine: errLine,\n        rawLines,\n        steps,\n        cfg,\n        finalResult: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    this.finalizeNextLines(steps);\n\n    return {\n      ok: true,\n      errorType: null,\n      errorMessage: null,\n      errorLine: null,\n      rawLines,\n      steps,\n      cfg,\n      finalResult: finalReturnVal !== null ? this.formatVal(finalReturnVal) : null\n    };\n  }\n\n  finalizeNextLines(steps) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < steps.length; i++) {\n      steps[i].nextLine = i + 1 < steps.length ? steps[i + 1].line : null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  stripInlineComment(line) {\n    let inSingle = false;\n    let inDouble = false;\n    for (let i = 0; i < line.length; i++) {\n      const ch = line[i];\n      if (ch === \"'\" && !inDouble) inSingle = !inSingle;\n      else if (ch === '\"' && !inSingle) inDouble = !inDouble;\n      else if (ch === \"#\" && !inSingle && !inDouble) {\n        return line.slice(0, i);\n      }\n    }\n    return line;\n  }\n\n  parseProgram(rawLines) {\n    const items = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < rawLines.length; i++) {\n      const stripped = this.stripInlineComment(rawLines[i]);\n      const trimmed = stripped.trim();\n      if (!trimmed) continue;\n      const indent = rawLines[i].match(/^\\s*/)[0].length;\n      items.push({ line: i + 1, indent, text: trimmed, raw: rawLines[i] });\n    }\n    return this.buildASTBlock(items, 0, items.length > 0 ? items[0].indent : 0).nodes;\n  }\n\n  buildASTBlock(items, startIdx, baseIndent) {\n    const nodes = [];\n    let i = startIdx;\n\n    while (i < items.length) {\n      const item = items[i];\n      if (item.indent < baseIndent) break;\n\n      if (item.text.startsWith(\"class \") && item.text.endsWith(\":\")) {\n        const className = item.text.slice(6, -1).split(\"(\")[0].trim();\n        const bodyRes = this.parseChildSuite(items, i + 1, item.indent);\n        nodes.push({\n          kind: \"CLASS\",\n          line: item.line,\n          text: item.text,\n          className,\n          body: bodyRes.nodes\n        });\n        i = bodyRes.nextIdx;\n      } else if (item.text.startsWith(\"def \") && item.text.endsWith(\":\")) {\n        // Support type annotations like `def maxSubArray(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:`\n        const match = item.text.match(/^def\\s+([a-zA-Z_]\\w*)\\s*\\((.*)\\)\\s*(?:->\\s*[^:]+)?\\s*:$/);\n        const funcName = match ? match[1] : \"func\";\n        const rawParams = match && match[2].trim() ? this.splitTopLevelArgs(match[2]) : [];\n        const params = rawParams\n          .map((p) => p.split(\":\")[0].trim())\n          .filter((p) => p && p !== \"self\");\n        const bodyRes = this.parseChildSuite(items, i + 1, item.indent);\n        nodes.push({\n          kind: \"DEF\",\n          line: item.line,\n          text: item.text,\n          funcName,\n          params,\n          body: bodyRes.nodes\n        });\n        i = bodyRes.nextIdx;\n      } else if (item.text.startsWith(\"if \") && item.text.endsWith(\":\")) {\n        const branches = [];\n        const cond = item.text.slice(3, -1).trim();\n        const bodyRes = this.parseChildSuite(items, i + 1, item.indent);\n        branches.push({\n          type: \"if\",\n          line: item.line,\n          text: item.text,\n          condition: cond,\n          body: bodyRes.nodes\n        });\n        i = bodyRes.nextIdx;\n\n        while (i < items.length && items[i].indent === item.indent) {\n          const cur = items[i];\n          if (cur.text.startsWith(\"elif \") && cur.text.endsWith(\":\")) {\n            const elifCond = cur.text.slice(5, -1).trim();\n            const elifBody = this.parseChildSuite(items, i + 1, cur.indent);\n            branches.push({\n              type: \"elif\",\n              line: cur.line,\n              text: cur.text,\n              condition: elifCond,\n              body: elifBody.nodes\n            });\n            i = elifBody.nextIdx;\n          } else if (cur.text === \"else:\") {\n            const elseBody = this.parseChildSuite(items, i + 1, cur.indent);\n            branches.push({\n              type: \"else\",\n              line: cur.line,\n              text: cur.text,\n              condition: null,\n              body: elseBody.nodes\n            });\n            i = elseBody.nextIdx;\n            break;\n          } else {\n            break;\n          }\n        }\n        nodes.push({\n          kind: \"IF_CHAIN\",\n          line: item.line,\n          text: item.text,\n          branches\n        });\n      } else if (item.text.startsWith(\"for \") && item.text.endsWith(\":\")) {\n        const header = item.text.slice(4, -1).trim();\n        const inIdx = header.indexOf(\" in \");\n        const iterVar = header.slice(0, inIdx).trim();\n        const iterExpr = header.slice(inIdx + 4).trim();\n        const bodyRes = this.parseChildSuite(items, i + 1, item.indent);\n        nodes.push({\n          kind: \"FOR\",\n          line: item.line,\n          text: item.text,\n          iterVar,\n          iterExpr,\n          body: bodyRes.nodes\n        });\n        i = bodyRes.nextIdx;\n      } else if (item.text.startsWith(\"while \") && item.text.endsWith(\":\")) {\n        const condition = item.text.slice(6, -1).trim();\n        const bodyRes = this.parseChildSuite(items, i + 1, item.indent);\n        nodes.push({\n          kind: \"WHILE\",\n          line: item.line,\n          text: item.text,\n          condition,\n          body: bodyRes.nodes\n        });\n        i = bodyRes.nextIdx;\n      } else {\n        nodes.push({\n          kind: \"STMT\",\n          line: item.line,\n          text: item.text\n        });\n        i++;\n      }\n    }\n\n    return { nodes, nextIdx: i };\n  }\n\n  parseChildSuite(items, nextIdx, parentIndent) {\n    if (nextIdx >= items.length || items[nextIdx].indent <= parentIndent) {\n      return { nodes: [], nextIdx };\n    }\n    return this.buildASTBlock(items, nextIdx, items[nextIdx].indent);\n  }\n\n  executeSuite(nodes, callStack, functions, classes, steps, stdout, loopStack) {\n    for (const node of nodes) {\n      if (steps.length >= this.maxSteps) {\n        throw {\n          line: node.line,\n          message: `TimeoutError: Execution exceeded ${this.maxSteps} steps (possible infinite loop).`\n        };\n      }\n      const res = this.executeNode(node, callStack, functions, classes, steps, stdout, loopStack);\n      if (res && (res.returned || res.broke || res.continued)) {\n        return res;\n      }\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  executeNode(node, callStack, functions, classes, steps, stdout, loopStack) {\n    const activeFrame = callStack[callStack.length - 1];\n\n    if (node.kind === \"CLASS\") {\n      classes[node.className] = { name: node.className, methods: {} };\n      steps.push({\n        stepIndex: steps.length + 1,\n        line: node.line,\n        codeText: node.text,\n        eventType: \"CLASS_DEF\",\n        functionName: activeFrame.frameName,\n        beforeVars: this.cloneVarsMap(activeFrame.vars),\n        variables: this.buildInspectorRows(activeFrame.vars, null),\n        changedVars: [],\n        changedSummary: `Defined class '${node.className}'`,\n        condition: null,\n        loop: this.getCurrentLoopSnapshot(loopStack),\n        operationDetail: { kind: \"class_def\", className: node.className },\n        returnValue: null,\n        stdout: [...stdout]\n      });\n\n      for (const child of node.body) {\n        if (child.kind === \"DEF\") {\n          classes[node.className].methods[child.funcName] = child;\n          functions[child.funcName] = child;\n          steps.push({\n            stepIndex: steps.length + 1,\n            line: child.line,\n            codeText: child.text,\n            eventType: \"METHOD_DEF\",\n            functionName: `class ${node.className}`,\n            beforeVars: this.cloneVarsMap(activeFrame.vars),\n       