{"step_index":48,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T10:25:31Z","input_tokens":18755,"cache_read_tokens":134851,"output_tokens":7796,"thinking":"Focusing on the creation of `explainer.js`, aiming to integrate rule-based teaching and a code questions engine. The goal is to ensure the explainer generates the required explanation items for each execution step, considering both beginner and technical modes. This file will be the core of the teaching system.\n\n\nThe `explainer.js` will rigorously detail the `maxSubArray` algorithm's execution step-by-step. The explanation will begin by outlining the context: the `Solution` class and method definition. Key variables, such as `c` (current subarray sum) and `ans` (best sum), their initial values, and roles will be explicitly stated.\n\nEach iteration of the loop will be unpacked: current index `i`, the element `nums[i]`, the state of `c` before and after adding `nums[i]`, and the logic behind condition `c >= ans` or `c < 0`, and the consequences of those conditions. The reasoning aims to provide insights on how `ans` is updated and why `c` resets when negative.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// explainer.js — Separated Rule-Based Teaching System, Symbol Dictionary & Built-In Questions Engine\n// 100% Rule-Based & Deterministic. Zero AI APIs.\n\nconst PYTHON_SYMBOLS_LIBRARY = [\n  { token: \"class\", label: \"class\", desc: \"Defines a class blueprint (`class Solution:`) that groups related methods together.\" },\n  { token: \"def\", label: \"def\", desc: \"Defines a function or method. Its body only runs when the function is called.\" },\n  { token: \"->\", label: \"->\", desc: \"Return type annotation indicating what type of value the function returns (e.g., `-> int`).\" },\n  { token: \"list[int]\", label: \"list[int]\", desc: \"Type hint meaning a list whose elements are integers.\" },\n  { token: \"for\", label: \"for\", desc: \"Starts a loop that repeats its indented block for each value in a sequence.\" },\n  { token: \"while\", label: \"while\", desc: \"Starts a loop that repeats as long as its condition evaluates to `True`.\" },\n  { token: \"range(\", label: \"range(n)\", desc: \"Generates integer indices from `0` up to `n - 1`.\" },\n  { token: \"len(\", label: \"len(nums)\", desc: \"Returns the number of elements in the list `nums`.\" },\n  { token: \"+=\", label: \"+=\", desc: \"Addition-assignment: adds the right-hand value to the variable on the left and saves the result back in that variable (`c += nums[i]` means `c = c + nums[i]`).\" },\n  { token: \"-=\", label: \"-=\", desc: \"Subtraction-assignment: subtracts the right-hand value from the variable on the left.\" },\n  { token: \">=\", label: \">=\", desc: \"Comparison operator: evaluates to `True` if the left value is greater than or equal to the right value.\" },\n  { token: \"<=\", label: \"<=\", desc: \"Comparison operator: evaluates to `True` if the left value is less than or equal to the right value.\" },\n  { token: \"==\", label: \"==\", desc: \"Equality operator: evaluates to `True` if both sides have the exact same value.\" },\n  { token: \"!=\", label: \"!=\", desc: \"Inequality operator: evaluates to `True` if the two sides are different.\" },\n  { token: \"<\", label: \"<\", desc: \"Less-than operator: evaluates to `True` if the left value is strictly less than the right value (`c < 0` checks if `c` is negative).\" },\n  { token: \">\", label: \">\", desc: \"Greater-than operator: evaluates to `True` if the left value is strictly greater than the right value.\" },\n  { token: \"=\", label: \"=\", desc: \"Assignment operator: evaluates the right side first and stores that value in the variable on the left.\" },\n  { token: \"[\", label: \"nums[i]\", desc: \"List indexing: reads the element at position `i` (0-based) from the list.\" },\n  { token: \"return\", label: \"return\", desc: \"Exits the current function immediately and sends the result back to the caller.\" },\n  { token: \"break\", label: \"break\", desc: \"Exits the enclosing `for` or `while` loop immediately.\" },\n  { token: \"continue\", label: \"continue\", desc: \"Skips the remaining lines of the current loop iteration and jumps to the next pass.\" }\n];\n\nclass RuleBasedExplainer {\n  enrichTraceWithExplanations(traceResult) {\n    if (!traceResult || !traceResult.steps) return traceResult;\n    const steps = traceResult.steps;\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < steps.length; i++) {\n      const step = steps[i];\n      const prevStep = i > 0 ? steps[i - 1] : null;\n      const nextStep = i + 1 < steps.length ? steps[i + 1] : null;\n      step.explanations = this.buildStepExplanation(step, prevStep, nextStep);\n      step.practiceQuestion = this.buildPracticeChallenge(step, nextStep);\n    }\n\n    traceResult.executionSummary = this.buildExecutionSummary(traceResult);\n    return traceResult;\n  }\n\n  buildStepExplanation(step, prevStep, nextStep) {\n    const code = step.codeText || \"\";\n    const op = step.operationDetail || {};\n    const cond = step.condition;\n    const beforeVars = step.beforeVars || {};\n\n    let whatBeginner = \"\";\n    let whatTechnical = \"\";\n\n    // 1. What the current line does (Beginner & Technical)\n    if (step.eventType === \"CLASS_DEF\") {\n      whatBeginner = `Creates a class named \\`${op.className}\\`. Think of a class as a container that holds methods (functions). Creating the class does not run the method code yet.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Executes \\`class ${op.className}:\\` definition in \\`${step.functionName}\\`, allocating the class namespace before method registration.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"METHOD_DEF\" || step.eventType === \"FUNC_DEF\") {\n      whatBeginner = `Defines the method \\`${op.funcName}(${(op.params || []).join(\", \")})\\`. Python records where this method is located, and waits until the method is called to run the lines inside it.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Registers function/method object \\`${op.funcName}\\` with formal parameters \\`(${(op.params || []).join(\", \")})\\`. The body is not executed at definition time.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"FUNC_CALL\") {\n      const bindingsStr = (op.paramBindings || [])\n        .map((b) => `\\`${b.param} = ${b.val}\\``)\n        .join(\", \");\n      whatBeginner = `Calls \\`${op.funcName}()\\` and passes the input into its parameter: ${bindingsStr}. Now Python enters the method body and starts running its lines one by one!`;\n      whatTechnical = `Invokes \\`${op.funcName}\\`, pushing a new stack frame \\`${step.functionName}\\` and binding argument values to local parameters (${bindingsStr}).`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_ITER\" && op.kind === \"for_iter\") {\n      const extraIdx = op.indexedElementInfo\n        ? ` At this index, \\`${op.indexedElementInfo.arrayName}[${op.indexedElementInfo.indexVal}]\\` is \\`${op.indexedElementInfo.elementVal}\\`.`\n        : \"\";\n      whatBeginner = `Starts **loop iteration ${op.iteration} of ${op.total}**: Python sets the loop variable \\`${op.iterVar} = ${op.iterVal}\\`.${extraIdx}`;\n      whatTechnical = `\\`for\\` loop iterator advances to pass ${op.iteration}/${op.total}, binding \\`${op.iterVar} = ${op.iterVal}\\` in local scope.${extraIdx}`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_END\") {\n      whatBeginner = `The loop has finished checking every item in the sequence. Python now exits the loop and moves to the line after the loop.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Loop iterator exhausted after ${op.total || \"all\"} iterations; control transfers past the loop suite.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"AUG_ASSIGN\") {\n      const resetContext =\n        op.target === \"c\"\n          ? ` (\\`c\\` tracks the current candidate subarray sum; adding \\`${op.rhsExpr}\\` updates our running candidate sum from \\`${op.beforeVal}\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`.)`\n          : \"\";\n      whatBeginner = `Python adds \\`${op.rhsExpr}\\` (\\`${op.rhsVal}\\`) to \\`${op.target}\\` (which was \\`${op.beforeVal}\\`): \\`${op.beforeVal} ${op.baseOp} (${op.rhsVal}) = ${op.afterVal}\\`, and stores \\`${op.afterVal}\\` back in \\`${op.target}\\`.${resetContext}`;\n      whatTechnical = `Augmented assignment \\`${code}\\` evaluates \\`${op.target} ${op.baseOp} ${op.rhsExpr}\\` (\\`${op.beforeVal} ${op.baseOp} ${op.rhsVal} -> ${op.afterVal}\\`) and updates \\`${op.target}\\` in place.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"ASSIGN\") {\n      let specialNote = \"\";\n      if (op.target === \"c\" && op.afterVal === \"0\" && !op.isCreated) {\n        specialNote = ` Resetting \\`c = 0\\` discards the negative candidate sum so it won't reduce the sum of future subarrays.`;\n      } else if (op.target === \"c\" && op.isCreated) {\n        specialNote = ` \\`c\\` will track our current candidate contiguous subarray sum.`;\n      } else if (op.target === \"ans\" && op.isCreated) {\n        specialNote = ` \\`ans\\` tracks the best subarray sum found so far. Initializing \\`ans = nums[0]\\` (${op.afterVal}) ensures the code works even if every number in \\`nums\\` is negative!`;\n      } else if (op.target === \"ans\" && !op.isCreated) {\n        specialNote = ` Because our current sum \\`c\\` (${op.afterVal}) beat or tied the previous best \\`ans\\` (${op.beforeVal}), \\`ans\\` is updated to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`!`;\n      }\n      whatBeginner = op.isCreated\n        ? `A variable named \\`${op.target}\\` is created and assigned the value \\`${op.afterVal}\\`.${specialNote}`\n        : `Variable \\`${op.target}\\` is updated from \\`${op.beforeVal}\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\` (from \\`${op.rhsExpr}\\`).${specialNote}`;\n      whatTechnical = `Assignment \\`${code}\\` evaluates RHS \\`${op.rhsExpr}\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\` and ${op.isCreated ? \"initializes\" : \"rebinds\"} local identifier \\`${op.target}\\`.${specialNote}`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"CONDITION\" && cond) {\n      const outcomeStr = cond.result ? \"True\" : \"False\";\n      let kadaneNote = \"\";\n      if (cond.expr === \"c >= ans\") {\n        kadaneNote = cond.result\n          ? ` Since candidate sum \\`c\\` (${cond.leftVal}) is at least as large as our best sum \\`ans\\` (${cond.rightVal}), Python will enter the \\`if\\` block to update \\`ans\\`!`\n          : ` Since candidate sum \\`c\\` (${cond.leftVal}) is smaller than our best sum \\`ans\\` (${cond.rightVal}), \\`ans\\` stays unchanged and Python skips the \\`if\\` block.`;\n      } else if (cond.expr === \"c < 0\") {\n        kadaneNote = cond.result\n          ? ` Since \\`c\\` (${cond.leftVal}) is negative, keeping it would only hurt future subarray sums—so Python enters the \\`if\\` block to reset \\`c = 0\\`.`\n          : ` Since \\`c\\` (${cond.leftVal}) is not negative, we keep accumulating \\`c\\` and skip the reset block.`;\n      }\n      whatBeginner = `Compares \\`${cond.expr}\\` using current values: \\`${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}\\` evaluates to **${outcomeStr}**.${kadaneNote}`;\n      whatTechnical = `Evaluates relational predicate \\`${cond.expr}\\` with operands \\`${cond.leftExpr}=${cond.leftVal}\\` and \\`${cond.rightExpr}=${cond.rightVal}\\`, yielding boolean \\`${outcomeStr}\\`.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"RETURN\") {\n      whatBeginner = `The function sends the current value of \\`${op.expr}\\` (\\`${op.returnVal}\\`) back to the code that called the function and finishes execution!`;\n      whatTechnical = `\\`return ${op.expr}\\` unwinds activation frame \\`${step.functionName}\\` and returns value \\`${op.returnVal}\\` to the caller.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"PRINT\") {\n      whatBeginner = `Prints \\`\"${op.output}\"\\` to the console output panel.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Writes formatted evaluation string \\`\"${op.output}\"\\` to standard output (\\`stdout\\`).`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"BREAK\") {\n      whatBeginner = `\\`break\\` immediately stops the current loop and jumps past the loop body.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Executes \\`break\\`, terminating the innermost enclosing loop suite.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"CONTINUE\") {\n      whatBeginner = `\\`continue\\` skips the rest of the current loop pass and jumps straight to the next iteration.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Executes \\`continue\\`, transferring control to the loop header for the next iteration.`;\n    } else if (step.eventType === \"EXCEPTION\") {\n      whatBeginner = `Execution stopped because of an error on this line: \\`${op.message}\\`.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Unhandled runtime exception raised: \\`${op.message}\\`.`;\n    } else {\n      whatBeginner = `Executes \\`${code}\\` on Line ${step.line}.`;\n      whatTechnical = `Executes statement \\`${code}\\` at line ${step.line} in scope \\`${step.functionName}\\`.`;\n    }\n\n    // 2. What the important symbols mean\n    const symbolsMeaning = this.explainSymbolsInLine(code);\n\n    // 3. Why this line is executing\n    const whyExecuting = this.explainWhyLineExecutes(step, prevStep);\n\n    // 4. What the variables contain before execution\n    const beforeKeys = Object.keys(beforeVars);\n    const variablesBefore =\n      beforeKeys.length === 0\n        ? \"No local variables existed in this scope before this line ran.\"\n        : beforeKeys.map((k) => `\\`${k} = ${beforeVars[k]}\\``).join(\", \");\n\n    // 5. What changes after execution\n    const whatChangesAfter = step.changedSummary || \"No variable values changed.\";\n\n    // 6. Why a condition is True or False\n    let whyCondition = \"This line is not a conditional check (`if` / `elif` / `while`).\";\n    if (cond) {\n      if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_ITER\" && op.kind === \"for_iter\") {\n        whyCondition = `True because index pass ${op.iteration} is within the sequence length (${op.total}), assigning \\`${op.iterVar} = ${op.iterVal}\\`.`;\n      } else if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_END\") {\n        whyCondition = `False because all ${op.total || \"\"} items in the sequence have been processed.`;\n      } else {\n        whyCondition = `\\`${cond.expr}\\` substituted \\`${cond.leftExpr} = ${cond.leftVal}\\` and \\`${cond.rightExpr} = ${cond.rightVal}\\`. Comparing \\`${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}\\` is **${cond.result ? \"True\" : \"False\"}**.`;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // 7. Which line executes next and why\n    const whatNext = this.explainWhatHappensNext(step, nextStep);\n\n    return {\n      whatBeginner,\n      whatTechnical,\n      symbolsMeaning,\n      whyExecuting,\n      variablesBefore,\n      whatChangesAfter,\n      whyCondition,\n      whatNext\n    };\n  }\n\n  explainSymbolsInLine(codeText) {\n    const matches = [];\n    for (const item of PYTHON_SYMBOLS_LIBRARY) {\n      if (codeText.includes(item.token)) {\n        matches.push(`• \\`${item.label}\\`: ${item.desc}`);\n      }\n    }\n    if (matches.length === 0) {\n      return \"• Standard Python variable or expression evaluation.\";\n    }\n    return matches.slice(0, 3).join(\"<br>\");\n  }\n\n  explainWhyLineExecutes(step, prevStep) {\n    if (!prevStep) {\n      return `Line ${step.line} executes first because Python reads the file from top to bottom starting at the first statement.`;\n    }\n    if (step.eventType === \"FUNC_CALL\") {\n      return `The class and method definitions finished registering, and the runner invoked \\`${step.operationDetail.funcName}(nums)\\` with the current input.`;\n    }\n    if (prevStep.eventType === \"FUNC_CALL\") {\n      return `Because \\`${prevStep.functionName}\\` was just called, Python jumped to the first line inside its body (Line ${step.line}).`;\n    }\n    if (prevStep.eventType === \"CONDITION\" && prevStep.condition) {\n      if (prevStep.condition.result) {\n        return `Because the condition \\`${prevStep.condition.expr}\\` on Line ${prevStep.line} was **True**, Python stepped inside the indented \\`if\\` block to run Line ${step.line}.`;\n      }\n      return `Because the condition \\`${prevStep.condition.expr}\\` on Line ${prevStep.line} was **False**, Python skipped the indented block and moved to Line ${step.line}.`;\n    }\n    if (prevStep.eventType === \"LOOP_ITER\") {\n      return `Because the loop on Line ${prevStep.line} started iteration #${prevStep.loop ? prevStep.loop.currentIteration : 1}, Python entered the indented loop body at Line ${step.line}.`;\n    }\n    if (prevStep.eventType === \"LOOP_END\") {\n      return `Because the loop on Line ${prevStep.line} finished all iterations, Python exited the loop and moved to Line ${step.line}.`;\n    }\n    if (step.line < prevStep.line) {\n      return `Line ${prevStep.line} completed the current pass of the loop body, so Python jumped **back up** to the loop header on Line ${step.line} for the next iteration.`;\n    }\n    return `Sequential execution: after completing Line ${prevStep.line}, Python moved down to the next statement on Line ${step.line}.`;\n  }\n\n  explainWhatHappensNext(step, nextStep) {\n    if (!nextStep) {\n      return `Program execution is complete! No more lines remain.`;\n    }\n    if (step.eventType === \"CONDITION\" && step.condition) {\n      return step.condition.result\n        ? `Because the condition is **True**, Python will enter the indented block at **Line ${nextStep.line}** (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`).`\n        : `Because the condition is **False**, Python skips the indented block and jumps to **Line ${nextStep.line}** (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`).`;\n    }\n    if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_ITER\") {\n      return `Python enters the loop body at **Line ${nextStep.line}** (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`).`;\n    }\n    if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_END\") {\n      return `Python exits the loop and jumps to **Line ${nextStep.line}** (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`).`;\n    }\n    if (nextStep.line < step.line) {\n      return `Having reached the end of the loop pass, Python jumps back up to the loop header on **Line ${nextStep.line}** (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`).`;\n    }\n    return `Execution moves to **Line ${nextStep.line}** (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`).`;\n  }\n\n  buildPracticeChallenge(step, nextStep) {\n    if (!nextStep) return null;\n    if (nextStep.eventType === \"CONDITION\" && nextStep.condition) {\n      const c = nextStep.condition;\n      return {\n        prompt: `Practice Prediction: On the next step (Line ${nextStep.line}: \\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`), what will \\`${c.expr}\\` evaluate to?`,\n        options: [\n          { label: `True (${c.leftVal} ${c.operator} ${c.rightVal} is True)`, correct: c.result === true },\n          { label: `False (${c.leftVal} ${c.operator} ${c.rightVal} is False)`, correct: c.result === false }\n        ],\n        explanation: `With \\`${c.leftExpr} = ${c.leftVal}\\` and \\`${c.rightExpr} = ${c.rightVal}\\`, \\`${c.leftVal} ${c.operator} ${c.rightVal}\\` evaluates to **${c.result ? \"True\" : \"False\"}**.`\n      };\n    }\n    if (\n      (nextStep.eventType === \"ASSIGN\" || nextStep.eventType === \"AUG_ASSIGN\") &&\n      nextStep.changedVars &&\n      nextStep.changedVars.length > 0\n    ) {\n      const targetName = nextStep.changedVars[0].name;\n      const row = nextStep.variables.find((v) => v.name === targetName);\n      if (row) {\n        const actual = row.current;\n        const numVal = Number(actual);\n        const opt1 = !Number.isNaN(numVal) ? String(numVal + 2) : `\"None\"`;\n        const opt2 = !Number.isNaN(numVal) ? String(numVal - 1) : `0`;\n        const options = [\n          { label: `${targetName} = ${actual}`, correct: true },\n          { label: `${targetName} = ${opt1}`, correct: false },\n          { label: `${targetName} = ${opt2}`, correct: false }\n        ].sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5);\n        return {\n          prompt: `Practice Prediction: After Line ${nextStep.line} (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`) executes, what will \\`${targetName}\\` be?`,\n          options,\n          explanation: `Line ${nextStep.line} sets \\`${nextStep.changedSummary}\\`.`\n        };\n      }\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  buildExecutionSummary(traceResult) {\n    if (!traceResult.ok || !traceResult.steps.length) {\n      return `Execution stopped before completion: ${traceResult.errorMessage || \"Check syntax or input.\"}`;\n    }\n    const steps = traceResult.steps;\n    const lastStep = steps[steps.length - 1];\n    const totalSteps = steps.length;\n    const ansUpdates = steps.filter(\n      (s) =>\n        (s.eventType === \"ASSIGN\" || s.eventType === \"AUG_ASSIGN\") &&\n        s.changedVars &&\n        s.changedVars.some((c) => c.name === \"ans\")\n    );\n    const resets = steps.filter(\n      (s) =>\n        s.eventType === \"ASSIGN\" &&\n        s.operationDetail &&\n        s.operationDetail.target === \"c\" &&\n        s.operationDetail.afterVal === \"0\" &&\n        !s.operationDetail.isCreated\n    );\n\n    if (traceResult.finalResult !== null) {\n      return `Completed in **${totalSteps} steps**. Final returned value: **\\`${traceResult.finalResult}\\`**. During execution, best answer \\`ans\\` was initialized/updated **${ansUpdates.length} time(s)**, and candidate sum \\`c\\` was reset to \\`0\\` **${resets.length} time(s)** when it became negative.`;\n    }\n    if (lastStep.stdout && lastStep.stdout.length > 0) {\n      return `Completed in **${totalSteps} steps**. Console output: \\`${lastStep.stdout.join(\" | \")}\\`.`;\n    }\n    return `Completed in **${totalSteps} steps**.`;\n  }\n\n  answerBuiltInQuestion(questionId, step, traceResult) {\n    if (!step) {\n      return \"Run or analyze the code first to inspect a step.\";\n    }\n    const exp = step.explanations;\n    const cond = step.condition;\n    const op = step.operationDetail || {};\n\n    switch (questionId) {\n      case \"what_line_does\":\n        return `**What Line ${step.line} (\\`${step.codeText}\\`) does:** ${exp.whatBeginner}`;\n\n      case \"why_var_changed\":\n        if (!step.changedVars || step.changedVars.length === 0) {\n          return `**Why no variable changed on Step ${step.stepIndex}:** Line ${step.line} (\\`${step.codeText}\\`) is a \\`${step.eventType}\\` step, which checks control flow or definitions without modifying variable values.`;\n        }\n        return `**Why variable changed on Step ${step.stepIndex}:** ${exp.whatChangesAfter}. ${exp.whatBeginner}`;\n\n      case \"why_cond_true\":\n        if (!cond) {\n          return `Line ${step.line} (\\`${step.codeText}\\`) does not evaluate a True/False condition. Step to an \\`if\\`, \\`elif\\`, \\`for\\`, or \\`while\\` line to inspect a condition.`;\n        }\n        if (!cond.result) {\n          return `On Step ${step.stepIndex}, the condition \\`${cond.expr}\\` actually evaluated to **False** (not True), because \\`${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}\\` is False.`;\n        }\n        return `**Why \\`${cond.expr}\\` is True on Step ${step.stepIndex}:** ${exp.whyCondition}`;\n\n      case \"why_cond_false\":\n        if (!cond) {\n          return `Line ${step.line} (\\`${step.codeText}\\`) does not evaluate a True/False condition. Step to an \\`if\\`, \\`elif\\`, \\`for\\`, or \\`while\\` line to inspect a condition.`;\n        }\n        if (cond.result) {\n          return `On Step ${step.stepIndex}, the condition \\`${cond.expr}\\` actually evaluated to **True** (not False), because \\`${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}\\` is True.`;\n        }\n        return `**Why \\`${cond.expr}\\` is False on Step ${step.stepIndex}:** ${exp.whyCondition}`;\n\n      case \"what_happens_next\":\n        return `**What happens next:** ${exp.whatNext}`;\n\n      case \"why_loop_repeat\":\n        if (!step.loop) {\n          return `Execution is not currently inside a loop on Step ${step.stepIndex}.`;\n        }\n        if (step.loop.isFinished) {\n          return `**Why the loop stopped:** All ${step.loop.totalIterations} items in \\`${step.loop.iterExpr}\\` have been visited, so the loop exits.`;\n        }\n        return `**Why the loop repeated (Iteration ${step.loop.currentIteration}${step.loop.totalIterations ? \" of \" + step.loop.totalIterations : \"\"}):** The loop continues as long as there are remaining items in \\`${step.loop.iterExpr || step.loop.condition}\\`. Currently \\`${step.loop.iterVar || \"condition\"} = ${step.loop.currentItemValue || \"True\"}\\`.`;\n\n      case \"why_return_value\": {\n        const retStep =\n          step.eventType === \"RETURN\"\n            ? step\n            : [...traceResult.steps].reverse().find((s) => s.eventType === \"RETURN\");\n        if (!retStep) {\n          return `This program does not execute a \\`return\\` statement.`;\n        }\n        return `**Why the function returns \\`${retStep.returnValue}\\` (on Step ${retStep.stepIndex}, Line ${retStep.line}):** At the end of the function, \\`${retStep.operationDetail.expr}\\` holds \\`${retStep.returnValue}\\`, which is the best maximum subarray sum accumulated across all loop iterations.`;\n      }\n\n      case \"what_if_change_input\":\n        return `**What happens if you change the input?** Use the **Input Playground** bar above! For example, try \\`nums = [-5, -2, -8]\\` (all negative numbers) to see why initializing \\`ans = nums[0]\\` returns \\`-2\\`, or try \\`nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]\\` to see \\`c\\` accumulate to \\`10\\` without ever resetting to \\`0\\`.`;\n\n      case \"what_symbol_means\":\n        return `**Symbols on Line ${step.line} (\\`${step.codeText}\\`):**<br>${exp.symbolsMeaning}`;\n\n      default:\n        return \"This question is outside the built-in rule-based explanation library.\";\n    }\n  }\n\n  explainVariableClick(varName, step, traceResult) {\n    const history = [];\n    traceResult.steps.forEach((s) => {\n      const v = (s.variables || []).find((row) => row.name === varName);\n      if (v && (v.status === \"created\" || v.status === \"updated\")) {\n        history.push(`Step ${s.stepIndex} (L${s.line}): \\`${v.previous}\\` → \\`${v.current}\\``);\n      }\n    });\n\n    const curRow = (step.variables || []).find((r) => r.name === varName);\n    const curVal = curRow ? curRow.current : \"not in scope\";\n    const roleMap = {\n      nums: \"The input list of numbers passed into the method.\",\n      c: \"Tracks the current candidate contiguous subarray sum. Resets to `0` whenever it drops below `0`.\",\n      ans: \"Tracks the maximum subarray sum seen so far across all iterations.\",\n      i: \"Loop index variable stepping from `0` to `len(nums) - 1`.\"\n    };\n    const role = roleMap[varName] || `Variable of type \\`${curRow ? curRow.type : \"unknown\"}\\` in \\`${step.functionName}\\`.`;\n\n    return `**Variable \\`${varName}\\` (Current value: \\`${curVal}\\`):** ${role}<br>**Change History:** ${history.length ? history.join(\" | \") : \"No changes recorded.\"}`;\n  }\n}\n\nwindow.RuleBasedExplainer = RuleBasedExplainer;\n","Description":"Create explainer.js with the 7-part Rule-Based Teaching System, Symbol Library, Practice Mode generator, and Built-In Code Questions engine","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\explainer.js","toolAction":"Creating rule-based explainer explainer.js","toolSummary":"Create explainer.js for rule-based explanations and built-in questions"}}]}
